\title{A quantity that is what an option entry filled times that option's delta}
\description{
The \code{parent_fill_delta} quantity of a plan: what a \code{then} join's first plan filled, scaled by the delta of the option the plan trades.

It is for a delta hedge. The plan's own instrument must be an option, or UBI refuses the plan, and at each fill UBI works out the option's Black-76 delta at \code{volatility} percent, using the last price of the order's own instrument, usually the future, as the forward. The order must be a \code{then} join's child (\code{parent_fill_needs_then}), and an order with side \code{against_delta} must have this quantity (\code{against_delta_needs_delta}); that side sells against a bought call and buys against a bought put. With \code{whole_lots} the size is rounded to whole lots of the order's own instrument. An expired option, or a forward with no price, leaves the size as it was, and UBI tries again on every tick until the order has started. An order sized this way that names an instrument the first plan trades is refused with HTTP 400, because it would only trade back what was filled.
}
